1
00:00:04,719 --> 00:00:08,638
If you're anything like me, you love Final Girl.

2
00:00:08,638 --> 00:00:16,449
But every Killer and every Location brings its own rules, its own setup and its own exceptions, and juggling them gets

3
00:00:16,449 --> 00:00:19,102
in the way of actually playing.

4
00:00:20,870 --> 00:00:24,562
So what if your phone could carry all of that for you?

5
00:00:24,562 --> 00:00:32,092
Every rule, card and reminder you need, at the moment you need it. That's the Final Girl Rules Assistant.

6
00:00:34,686 --> 00:00:39,868
Final Girl is a solo horror board game from Van Ryder Games.

7
00:00:39,868 --> 00:00:48,647
You are the last survivor in a slasher film. Rescue the victims, find a weapon, and destroy the Killer, before it destroys you.

8
00:00:50,403 --> 00:00:54,909
The Core Box holds the player board, dice and Action cards.

9
00:00:54,909 --> 00:01:02,356
Each Feature Film box adds one Killer and one Location, and any Killer can hunt in any Location.

10
00:01:04,103 --> 00:01:11,598
Your board tracks your health, your Horror, which sets how many dice you roll, and the Time you spend on every action.

11
00:01:13,170 --> 00:01:18,438
Each Killer brings a board, a Bloodlust track, Dark Powers and a Finale.

12
00:01:18,438 --> 00:01:24,173
Each Location brings its own map, Item decks, Events and Terror cards.

13
00:01:25,936 --> 00:01:33,593
And then come the special rules. The Evomorph evolves, vanishes and ambushes. The Konrad adds Keycards, maintenance

14
00:01:33,593 --> 00:01:35,911
shafts and a self-destruct.

15
00:01:35,911 --> 00:01:40,676
Across three series, that's a great deal to remember in the dark.

16
00:01:43,286 --> 00:01:46,271
The home screen is your way in.

17
00:01:46,271 --> 00:01:51,684
Start Setup, track a turn, or jump straight to any of the fifteen tabs.

18
00:01:53,436 --> 00:01:59,547
Every screen reshapes itself around the Killer, Location and Final Girl you pick.

19
00:01:59,547 --> 00:02:02,878
So we'll follow three very different nights.

20
00:02:02,878 --> 00:02:10,714
Laurie against Hans the Butcher at Camp Happy Trails. Ellen against the Evomorph aboard the USS Konrad.

21
00:02:10,714 --> 00:02:17,699
And Selena, facing the Poltergeist in the Sacred Groves: a pairing the game never intended.

22
00:02:20,319 --> 00:02:25,525
Setup Assist walks you through the whole setup, and remembers where you are.

23
00:02:25,525 --> 00:02:30,456
For Hans at Camp Happy Trails, there's no special setup at all.

24
00:02:32,203 --> 00:02:36,798
Switch to the Evomorph on the Konrad, and a new section appears.

25
00:02:36,798 --> 00:02:44,152
Start Evolution at Hatchling. Build an eight-card Terror deck, not ten. Prepare the Ambush deck. Place the Keycards,

26
00:02:44,152 --> 00:02:47,478
the Super Loader and the Maintenance cards.

27
00:02:49,236 --> 00:02:53,718
Choose the Poltergeist in the Groves, and it changes again.

28
00:02:53,718 --> 00:03:03,055
Hide Carolyn and Mister Floppy in the Item decks, because the only way to win is to rescue Carolyn. Then set up Divine Wrath.

29
00:03:03,055 --> 00:03:07,508
Further down, the Item deck step now carries a warning.

30
00:03:09,269 --> 00:03:14,435
Even the Setup card you record comes from your Location's own list.

31
00:03:16,203 --> 00:03:22,329
And all of this lives on your phone, propped beside the board while you lay out the components.

32
00:03:25,719 --> 00:03:34,458
This Game gathers everything for tonight's pairing: art and flavour, your Final Girl's card, tips, icons and the rule sheets.

33
00:03:34,458 --> 00:03:38,331
For Hans, there are no special rules to remember.

34
00:03:40,069 --> 00:03:44,441
For the Evomorph on the Konrad, it's a very different page.

35
00:03:44,441 --> 00:03:50,877
It recognises the official scenario, and warns you about mistakes you've repeated before.

36
00:03:50,877 --> 00:04:00,052
Then it spells out the special rules in play. Evolution. Vanishing and Ambush. Scanning. Keycards, shafts and the self-destruct.

37
00:04:00,052 --> 00:04:06,077
Fourteen tips for this exact matchup follow, then the icons and the rule sheets.

38
00:04:07,836 --> 00:04:11,010
Mix and match, and it still keeps up.

39
00:04:11,010 --> 00:04:18,676
It flags that this isn't the canon pairing, then merges both rule sets. She can't be damaged, and you only win by

40
00:04:18,676 --> 00:04:20,688
escaping with Carolyn.

41
00:04:20,688 --> 00:04:27,420
While the Groves add Divine Wrath, where every increase also fires a second Bloodlust track.

42
00:04:30,020 --> 00:04:34,090
The Turn Tracker is your live dashboard at the table.

43
00:04:34,090 --> 00:04:41,974
Horror, Bloodlust, Time and Victims saved sit up top, and it works out your dice. Horror three means roll two.

44
00:04:41,974 --> 00:04:47,378
Each of the five phases shows what to do, and the reminders people forget.

45
00:04:49,136 --> 00:04:56,210
Here, the pairing really matters. With the Konrad in play, the Action phase gains a Keycard beat.

46
00:04:57,970 --> 00:05:05,236
In the Killer phase: while the Evomorph has vanished, skip the Killer Action, and draw an Ambush card instead.

47
00:05:07,003 --> 00:05:13,918
In the Groves, once the Finale is revealed, unleash Divine Wrath, then increase it by one.

48
00:05:15,670 --> 00:05:18,826
Logging events takes a tap or two.

49
00:05:18,826 --> 00:05:26,173
Tap Terror card, and it offers only the cards that can be in your deck, each with a preview of its effect.

50
00:05:26,173 --> 00:05:34,868
Hans's butcher and his campers. The Evomorph's ambushes. The Poltergeist's hauntings, and the angry gods of the Groves.

51
00:05:36,636 --> 00:05:41,506
Pick one, and its full effect appears, so you resolve it correctly.

52
00:05:43,270 --> 00:05:48,204
Dark Powers work the same way, including the Konrad's own Slippery.

53
00:05:49,970 --> 00:05:53,541
Items come from the Location's own decks.

54
00:05:53,541 --> 00:05:59,590
Note a mistake as it happens, and when the night is over, one button files the lot.

55
00:06:01,336 --> 00:06:10,310
At the table, it sits in your hand. Counters pinned at the top, the phase's beats beneath, and any card's effect one tap away.

56
00:06:13,720 --> 00:06:20,424
The Codex lets you browse every Killer, Location and Final Girl across all three series.

57
00:06:22,170 --> 00:06:26,647
Filter by name, and open At a Glance for the key rules.

58
00:06:28,403 --> 00:06:35,719
The Final Girls tab shows both sides of every card, so you can choose who suits the Killer you face.

59
00:06:38,320 --> 00:06:44,757
Ask a Question takes plain English, works offline, and tailors its answer to your game.

60
00:06:46,503 --> 00:06:53,771
Ask how Keycards work, and the Konrad's own rules, setup and tips come first, each with its source.

61
00:06:55,536 --> 00:07:01,549
Ask how to win against the Poltergeist, and it leads with the altered win condition.

62
00:07:03,303 --> 00:07:09,053
Mid-game, when you can't quite remember a rule, the answer is already in your pocket.

63
00:07:12,453 --> 00:07:17,811
The Game Log is your body count: every game, and whether you walked away.

64
00:07:17,811 --> 00:07:24,127
Open one, and you get The Story, a slasher-style recap written from the events you logged.

65
00:07:24,127 --> 00:07:28,325
Below it, the summary and the turn-by-turn timeline.

66
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:39,751
Scenarios is the Killer-by-Location grid. Green is beaten. Red is played, not yet beaten. Official pairings are starred.

67
00:07:42,353 --> 00:07:50,526
The M I tab turns your history into numbers: win rate, streaks, your best and worst matchups, and win rates by Killer,

68
00:07:50,526 --> 00:07:52,788
Location and Final Girl.

69
00:07:54,536 --> 00:07:59,414
After the game, it tells the story of the night, and keeps the score.

70
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:10,334
Achievements tracks every Killer and Location achievement. The ones your wins prove fill in by themselves.

71
00:08:12,953 --> 00:08:21,265
Debrief groups your mistakes, so repeat offenders rise to the top, and pulls out the ones to watch for in this matchup.

72
00:08:23,886 --> 00:08:29,497
Tips holds strategy advice, including the rules people most often get wrong,

73
00:08:31,236 --> 00:08:35,987
and opens on whichever Killer and Location you're playing.

74
00:08:38,586 --> 00:08:44,640
Rules Reference summarises the core rules in rulebook order, with page numbers,

75
00:08:46,403 --> 00:08:50,810
and you can search a word like Bloodlust to narrow it down.

76
00:08:53,420 --> 00:08:57,644
Icon Reference decodes every core card symbol.

77
00:08:59,403 --> 00:09:04,399
Below are the scenario icons for every Killer and Location.

78
00:09:04,399 --> 00:09:11,165
The Birds. The Groves' Divine Wrath. The Evomorph's Vanish and Scan. The Konrad's Keycards.

79
00:09:11,165 --> 00:09:16,925
Wolfe Asylum's pills. The Tormentor's death traps. The Hellscape's tiles.

80
00:09:19,520 --> 00:09:24,766
And Asset Admin keeps track of the artwork and the development backlog.

81
00:09:27,386 --> 00:09:31,223
Less time in the rulebook. More time in the dark.

82
00:09:31,223 --> 00:09:37,430
That's the Final Girl Rules Assistant. Now the only thing you need to worry about, is the Killer.
